commit 54253348eb48525afb438d66f681aff58af90308
Author: Mike Holownych <mike.holownych@aisyndicate.io>
Date:   Tue Nov 24 20:38:25 2026 +0000

    feat(schedules): fire schedules from the runner and add the nexus schedule commands

    BG-2 slice 2. The runner's schedule engine starts a job through the same acceptance as a client's start request
    (job_submission.ts is now shared by nexus job start and the engine). Missed slots are counted, reported once as a
    gap and a missed-run receipt, never replayed; run-once (default) starts one catch-up, report starts none. A slot due
    while the previous job runs is recorded as an overlap. A clock stepped backwards recomputes the next slot and never
    re-runs a slot. The job receipt gains schedule_occurrence and a filled-in missed (additive, version stays 1).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M87MFZ600A94G93A9NX2QMJ3

